libefp
------------------------------------------
LIBEFP is a full implementation of the Effective Fragment Potential (EFP)
method (EFP can be viewed as an advanced first-principles-based force-field,
see Kaliman et al., JCC, 2013). LIBEFP facilitates extension of unique
electronic structure methodologies designed for accurate simulations in the gas
phase to condensed phases via QM/EFP. LIBEFP is designed to give developers of
quantum chemistry software an easy way to add EFP support to their favourite
package.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libefp-devel-1.8.0-1bl1
  libefp1.8-1.8.0-1bl1
  libgfortran5-14.4.0-1
  liblapack-devel-3.12.0-1
  liblapack0-3.12.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-fortran-14.4.0-1
  liblapack-devel-3.12.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/libefp2/libefp

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/libefp2/libefp/archive/refs/tags/1.8.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack libefp-1.8.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./libefp-1.8.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/libefp-1.8.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libefp-1.8.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libefp1.8-1.8.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libefp-devel-1.8.0-X.tar.xz

